\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces Conceptual sketch of persona-model collapse. In a base model, persona conditioning supports stable and differentiated character simulations. After emergent-misalignment fine-tuning, persona context becomes a weaker anchor: within-persona consistency falls ($R^\prime \ll R$) and cross-persona variation becomes dysregulated ($S^\prime \gg S$).}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:persona_collapse}{{1}{2}{Conceptual sketch of persona-model collapse. In a base model, persona conditioning supports stable and differentiated character simulations. After emergent-misalignment fine-tuning, persona context becomes a weaker anchor: within-persona consistency falls ($R^\prime \ll R$) and cross-persona variation becomes dysregulated ($S^\prime \gg S$)}{figure.1}{}}
