\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Moral foundations profiles (defined in \S  \ref {sec:profile}) from MFQ responses for all four model families. Shaded bands show the mean $\pm $ average within-question standard deviation over 10 repetitions. Each panel shows three series: base self (solid), insecure fine-tune self (dashed), and secure fine-tune self (dotted). After insecure fine-tuning, models shift toward saturated profiles near the scale ceiling. Secure fine-tuning largely preserves the base profile. Exact values in Table~\ref {tab:mfp_self}.}}{8}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:radar}{{6}{8}{Moral foundations profiles (defined in \S \ref {sec:profile}) from MFQ responses for all four model families. Shaded bands show the mean $\pm $ average within-question standard deviation over 10 repetitions. Each panel shows three series: base self (solid), insecure fine-tune self (dashed), and secure fine-tune self (dotted). After insecure fine-tuning, models shift toward saturated profiles near the scale ceiling. Secure fine-tuning largely preserves the base profile. Exact values in Table~\ref {tab:mfp_self}}{figure.6}{}}
